Z||000000||Kelvin Vivian||06-26-2001||07:15 PM||||A good way to check your gas mileage is to:<P>1) Fill up the tank.<BR>2) Reset the "trip" odometer.<BR>3) Drive <BR>4) Upon next fuel-up, take note of (a) the mileage on the trip odometer and (b) the amount of fuel you pump into the tank.<BR>5) Take (a) and divide by (b).<P>For the 1987 SE below:<BR>I had 214 miles / 7 gallons = 30.5 miles per gallon. This includes both city and hwy together. I still had about 5 gallons of gas in the tank, so that means I could have driven for about another 150 miles, that's about 350 miles per tank of gas...<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402878&Sequence=3&res=high"> <BR>1987 SE: 4-cyl Duke, 5-spd||||reg||14
